# Soldering at the bench (decisions C17, C18): the DIP into the vise on
# the turntable; arm A brings a resistor's lead to pin 3's tip, square
# to the pin row; pincer P1 comes in from the turntable's side and grips
# the lead -- the turntable now holds the resistor, and A lets go and
# goes; the turntable turns and rises to present the joint to station
# S1, whose iron touches it and whose own feeder feeds the solder; the
# iron backs away, the joint freezes; P1 lets go and the resistor stays,
# soldered on.
reset circuit=demo
tool A tweezers
pick A U1 grasp=ends
place A U1 at=0,0,-24 rpy=0,0,90
vise close
release A U1
pick A R1 grasp=body
lift A mm=80
move A to=0,60,60 rpy=180,0,90
move A to=34.81,1.27,-14.05
align A R1.1.tip to=U1.3.tip gap=0.1
pinch P1 on=R1.1 at=6
release A R1
lift A mm=60
present U1.3+R1.1 at=S1
touch S1 at=U1.3+R1.1 dwell=2
feed S1 mm=2 rate=1
back S1
wait until=U1.3+R1.1 below=100
inspect U1.3+R1.1
unpinch P1
